4 1034 "I only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251744 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251744 1111 #uuid "1fdf86a3-cae6-5d09-a08c-2f3ae45fb149" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251745 1034 "III only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251745 1111 #uuid "93659e81-69d5-57eb-a2d0-3828ed1c7279" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251746 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251746 1111 #uuid "ba500de3-7e87-5ca0-8f56-e95d8df3a675" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251747 1034 "II only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251747 1111 #uuid "f0412890-d59e-5222-b528-ddd45e1cc8c3" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251749 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1089 "q-339585" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1100 "If $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=10$ and $g(10)=5,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\frac{g(x)-\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)}=$\n {{field-1}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1113 #uuid "3ef9c30f-4a7e-5e86-9fd3-8b9955c73729" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251748 1145 "Since $g(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}g(x)=g(10)=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\frac{g(x)-\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}g(x)-{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{+}}\\operatorname{log}⁡x}{3g(10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-\\operatorname{log}⁡10}{3(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{3(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251749 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251750 13194139533796 true] [17592186251749 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251749 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251749 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251750 13194139533796 true] [17592186251749 1110 #uuid "01aacdc2-7e87-599a-bde9-7f9c7ea4a42b" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251750 1034 "\\frac{4}{15}" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251750 1111 #uuid "0acdea37-b24e-5d1b-85c2-287592cf22dc" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251752 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1089 "q-339592" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1100 "If $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=5$ and $g(5)=5,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}\\frac{g(x)-{x}^{2}}{4x}=$\n {{field-1}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1113 #uuid "6c3e571a-4724-5af9-bcc0-f9ca20412934" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251751 1145 "Since $g(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=5,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)=g(5)=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}\\frac{g(x)-{x}^{2}}{4x} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}g(x)-\\text{ }{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}{x}^{2}}{{lim}_{x\\to {5}^{-}}4x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-{5}^{2}}{4(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-25}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251753 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251754 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251754 13194139533796 true] [17592186251752 1110 #uuid "a5c5832d-07e2-595d-afe1-ac6be838fa8e" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251753 1034 "1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251753 1111 #uuid "6f982f4b-0a43-5957-a096-7ed259b0a574" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251754 1034 "-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251754 1111 #uuid "bf7d4618-52eb-519a-b7d5-479a6da2c3a4" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251756 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1089 "q-339597" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1100 "If $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10$ and $h(10)=15,$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10))=$\n {{field-1}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1113 #uuid "224c62c3-d8c3-5a74-a48f-f28670c74d80" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251755 1145 "Since $h(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)=h(10)=15.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}(xh(x)-5h(10)) & ={lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}x\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(x)-5\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to {10}^{-}}h(10) \\\\  & =10\\cdot 15-5\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =150-75 \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251757 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251758 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251758 13194139533796 true] [17592186251756 1110 #uuid "23495c8d-030c-57a0-9a16-a93380bb783c" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251757 1034 "150" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251757 1111 #uuid "19d48e51-e895-517b-9a09-d87b29aaba2a" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251758 1034 "75" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251758 1111 #uuid "347740f4-fe94-500c-870d-738b6323e770" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251760 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251762 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1089 "q-341375" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/f223c6b96b4ce7e522d1529145ae90d7d68927e3234aa891a7be30a345355a9e.png)\n\nFrom **left to right**, the function $y=f(x)$ above is left-continuous but is not continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}} $\\,$ and  \n$\\,x=$\n {{field-2}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1113 #uuid "d7444952-e689-5026-9ea6-0702c532dc85" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251759 1145 "To determine whether $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-2,$ $x=1,$ and $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-2$ the function is not left-continuous because it's undefined at this point. $\\,\\times $\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)=2=f(1).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{-}}f(x)=0=f(3).\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, from **left to right**, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at $x=1$ and $x=3.$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251761 13194139533796 true] [17592186251760 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251760 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251760 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251761 13194139533796 true] [17592186251760 1110 #uuid "30f95881-1911-5674-bb10-e4c875e39d4d" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251761 1034 "1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251761 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251761 1111 #uuid "ea9ad21e-441b-55ea-8219-051fd4298f44" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251763 13194139533796 true] [17592186251762 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251762 1041 "field-2" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251762 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251763 13194139533796 true] [17592186251762 1110 #uuid "13031d09-e88f-5c61-bf6d-c5d64d7aedcb" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251763 1034 "3" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251763 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251763 1111 #uuid "b8960d1d-052a-50ff-88f3-364a4c6c5c23" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251765 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251767 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1089 "q-341379" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/f4f20d86a96988d657aeac166b6228cc938523e0ba6100908725aa83b6c88781.png)\n\nFrom **left to right**, the function $y=f(x)$ above is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}} $\\,$ and  \n$\\,x=$\n {{field-2}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1113 #uuid "e3dbf1cc-f8fe-5c56-b884-f7d15af77f72" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251764 1145 "To determine whether $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the right-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-3$, $x=-1,$ and $x=1.$\n\n- At $x=-3$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}f(x)=-2=f(-3).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is not right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}f(x)=0\\ne -2=f(-1).\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x)=0=f(1).\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, from **left to right**, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n$x=-3$ and $x=1.$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251765 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251766 13194139533796 true] [17592186251765 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251765 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251765 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251766 13194139533796 true] [17592186251765 1110 #uuid "36e772ba-52d9-52b3-a48e-7ddf83af5b76" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251766 1034 "-3" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251766 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251766 1111 #uuid "724420fc-6fa0-5034-b16a-c970cec521e2" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251767 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251768 13194139533796 true] [17592186251767 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251767 1041 "field-2" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251767 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251768 13194139533796 true] [17592186251767 1110 #uuid "fed81b16-5ce8-5842-85b3-f808e335dd19" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251768 1034 "1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251768 1111 #uuid "8c31086e-5f9d-542a-8ac5-193b4a7832dd" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251770 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1089 "q-341576" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/ef59e4b5c39770c5bcade3475a23d2631d2db10fea4fd7c925be092bbf819e61.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is not continuous but is right-continuous at\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1113 #uuid "2e581ab1-1c0e-5e8a-a3db-36c8d21f3746" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251769 1145 "To determine whether $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the right-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function has three discontinuities: $x=-1$ and $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{+}}f(x)=1=f(-1).\\,✓\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is not right-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(3).\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous but is right-continuous at $x=-1.$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251771 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251772 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1041 "field-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251772 13194139533796 true] [17592186251770 1110 #uuid "d0c78726-f95b-5d89-8616-a46065fdb064" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251771 1034 "3" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251771 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251771 1111 #uuid "488bc865-d437-563b-95d6-2139e3e2a8b5" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251772 1034 "-1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251772 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533796 true] [17592186251772 1111 #uuid "e454d8c9-2c04-513f-b191-f37b766975ec" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251774 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1089 "q-38546" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/8fdb835ed2998fae4d8afc3fd5e593bac6c72b1ee45c8b4fe01bdc4348322d1e.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\n- The function is continuous at $x=-1$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1113 #uuid "a73a0e01-eeb1-509f-a99b-e23afee7b7c1" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251773 1145 "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251775 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251776 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251777 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251778 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251779 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1041 "selection" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251775 13194139533796 true] [17592186251774 1110 #uuid "02cc2f62-69a0-5c27-8c1b-a68a79654228" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251775 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251775 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251775 1111 #uuid "124a9328-b83b-527a-a5ab-f1aa92890b9c" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251776 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251776 1111 #uuid "3afb8365-ed02-5316-b45a-395ca92a0387" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251777 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251777 1111 #uuid "ce6e9156-4ccf-53c2-bb5c-a1e91ccb29cf" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251778 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251778 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251778 1111 #uuid "8b6329c6-37d6-5df0-bab7-63762383b3ef" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251779 1034 "II only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251779 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251779 1111 #uuid "35e513e2-4478-554b-87f5-f313666b3fc3" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251780 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251781 13194139533796 true] [17592186251780 1089 "q-48272" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251780 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533796 true] [17592186251780 1100 "Which of the following functions is not continuous at $x=2$ but is right-continuous at that point?" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251780 1113 #uuid "abc90c9d-8ddb-5da3-8527-777