question-capture/13945035/assets/2153e8505d5962771a763be01e8fc3337f34516095a354b483e52d1171e0ee3c.png" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251784 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533796 true] [17592186251784 1111 #uuid "49a7dccd-efd4-501f-ad08-c44dc639f75d" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251785 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/b0c5521372b10882b6f5357cb678aef1274df935e7626bec930e3e084674ba62.png" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251785 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533796 true] [17592186251785 1111 #uuid "fd1844b7-b655-5430-b753-bc010280f31a" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251786 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/a8d239b7177df7deeebb363661bab5384ded495ae8cb0ccb7ec8e55531b9eb31.png" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251786 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139533796 true] [17592186251786 1111 #uuid "1ad2f3c7-5fbc-5544-b7c6-5f583145cf35" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251788 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1089 "q-73054" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/a025dc971bd0bb473e6b47f90b68ee8e8573a7acc8e5e879eab0173be1d41dcb.png)\n\nAt which points is the function $y=f(x)$ above left-continuous but is not continuous?" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1113 #uuid "23d077ae-b48b-5fdf-8116-b40f9d5a2533" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251787 1145 "To determine whether $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=c,$ we need to check whether the left-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nLet's check this for $x=-1$, at $x=1$ and at  $x=3.$\n\n- At $x=-1$ the function is not left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne -1=f(-1).\n$$\n\n- At $x=1$ the function is not left-continuous because \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)=-1\\ne 1=f(1).\n$$\n\n- At $x=3$ the function is left-continuous because\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{3}^{-}}f(x)=1=f(3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=3$ only." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251789 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251790 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251791 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251792 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251793 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1041 "selection" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251789 13194139533796 true] [17592186251788 1110 #uuid "99efa492-d17b-5f74-8def-5881e270cf91" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251789 1034 "$x=3$ only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251789 1111 #uuid "f72829e6-9b0c-5ffb-af82-22f6fe043c9b" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251790 1034 "$x=1$ only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251790 1111 #uuid "86f28d33-c9f1-586f-bb7e-be126639db77" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251791 1034 "$x=1$ and $x=3$ only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251791 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251791 1111 #uuid "990b81df-e422-5c50-94fa-05c0ae079607" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251792 1034 "$x=-1$ only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251792 1111 #uuid "d533677d-2133-54c8-b120-817beeccc476" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251793 1034 "$x=-1$ and $x=1$ only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251793 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251793 1111 #uuid "2f897499-a605-584e-8b8b-0ed17601335c" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251795 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1089 "q-73105" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/ad3fb8a0cce2a6dac706d7876aca0a2339fe49c05cb7aa6ae54de86735ceafab.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\n- The function is left-continuous at $x=3$\n- The function is right-continuous at $x=3$\n- The function is continuous at $x=3$" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1113 #uuid "260cf2f8-813c-5d74-b688-b2ee61ca37fd" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251794 1145 "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=3,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)=3\\ne 1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=3,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x)=1=f(3)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=3,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251796 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251797 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251798 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251799 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251800 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1041 "selection" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251800 13194139533796 true] [17592186251795 1110 #uuid "48a5fa4e-a100-5e3b-beb4-6c70178938b5" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251796 1034 "I only" 13194139533796 true] [17592186251796 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533796 true] [17592186251796 1111 #